  "slug": "expanding-glycomics-0644",
  "summary": "New tools rewrite or wrap analysis steps, from deepTools4 to CLIPittyClip, and harmonize public metadata to make large-scale reanalysis more tractable.",
  "synthesis": "The items share an infrastructure thread: reimplementing or packaging established analysis steps so they run faster, more reproducibly, and on public data. deepTools4 rewrites core functions in a modernized suite with benchmarked speed-ups, MAUDE-Py ports a probabilistic framework for sorting-based CRISPR screens to Python, and CLIPittyClip runs from raw FASTQ to peak matrices and crosslink sites with a 27-fold faster crosslink step (CLink). On the data-reuse side, MetaHQ harmonizes annotations from 13 curation sources for over 567k GEO samples, and Meta2Data standardizes retrieval and processing of public microbiome data from INSDC and CNCB. RSMViewer adds PyMOL-based batch visualization of RNA structural motifs. The novelty lies in engineering and usability rather than new algorithms. The proteomics and glycoproteomics emphasis from earlier is not supported by these items.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-14"
}
